1
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:41,439
Who the hell is it?

2
00:01:43,599 --> 00:01:44,280
Let me tell you, it's the middle of the night.

3
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,400
Quit playing tricks on me!

4
00:01:47,959 --> 00:01:49,040
I am a martial artist.

5
00:01:53,319 --> 00:01:54,920
Back in elementary school, I won

6
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,879
1st prize in a city martial arts contest.

7
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,640
I've written two martial arts manuals.

8
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,239
Seven or eight guys can't even touch me.

9
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,519
So what if you're a wild beast?

10
00:02:01,519 --> 00:02:02,920
Jackals, bears...

11
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:03,920
Even if you're a tiger...

12
00:02:04,439 --> 00:02:05,920
I'll kill you in three punches!

13
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,000
Try me if you don't believe it.

14
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,560
You think I'm...

15
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,240
A real tiger?!

16
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,560
Bro, I was just bluffing earlier, bro!

17
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,319
Mr. Fang, you... run!

18
00:02:57,319 --> 00:02:58,400
I'll hold it off!

19
00:03:06,039 --> 00:03:06,639
Bie Fan!

20
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,680
Just leave me!

21
00:03:09,639 --> 00:03:10,400
I've figured it out.

22
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,000
Getting killed by a tiger is still dying.

23
00:03:13,199 --> 00:03:14,800
Not a bad way to go. You leave!

24
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:16,680
Come here!

25
00:03:20,759 --> 00:03:22,240
Come chase me!

26
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,159
Chase me!

27
00:03:24,159 --> 00:03:24,680
Bie Fan!

28
00:03:25,599 --> 00:03:26,360
Come here, tiger. Look at me!

29
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,439
Today, either you kill me...

30
00:03:27,439 --> 00:03:28,000
...or I kill you!

31
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:28,479
Come on!

32
00:03:28,479 --> 00:03:30,360
I'm talking to you! Answer me!

33
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:31,120
Don't provoke it!

34
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,000
Are you deaf?

35
00:03:32,759 --> 00:03:34,039
You can't... You can't die! Eat me!

36
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,240
It's settled! Eat me!

37
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:37,520
His meat doesn't taste good!

38
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:38,120
Eat me! Come on!

39
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,879
He's over fifty!

40
00:03:39,879 --> 00:03:42,039
I'm young! My meat is tasty!

41
00:03:42,039 --> 00:03:43,599
Young meat is tough!

42
00:03:43,599 --> 00:03:44,879
Listen to me, tiger.

43
00:03:44,879 --> 00:03:45,680
Listen to me, tiger!

44
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,159
Can you just shut up?

45
00:03:47,159 --> 00:03:47,520
Eat me!

46
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,479
I'm trying really hard to save you!

47
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:50,400
I'll kick you to death!

48
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,280
You... Can't you...

49
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,000
...hear me?

50
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:52,639
Don't listen to him!

51
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,000
Come here!

52
00:04:00,199 --> 00:04:02,199
I don't think it understands.

53
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:25,800
I'll hit you.

54
00:04:39,879 --> 00:04:40,920
Mr. Fang.

55
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Thank you.

56
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:43,959
What are you doing here?

57
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,279
I was afraid you'd kill yourself.

58
00:04:48,279 --> 00:04:50,519
So I followed... kept following you.

59
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:54,319
I was afraid you'd kill yourself,

60
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,120
so I just kept following you.

61
00:05:02,519 --> 00:05:03,600
You still have a friend.

62
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:09,519
Bie Fan.

63
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,360
Bie Fan.

64
00:05:28,199 --> 00:05:29,120
Thanks.

65
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,560
You...

66
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:37,160
Didn't you already kiss that girl?

67
00:05:37,279 --> 00:05:38,439
Why did she leave?

68
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,399
Mr. Fang!

69
00:05:48,199 --> 00:05:50,040
Bro, eat some fruit.

70
00:05:51,439 --> 00:05:52,279
I'm telling you.

71
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,920
I'm not done with that tiger.

72
00:05:57,199 --> 00:05:57,839
To hell with it!

73
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,079
Why is it so sour?

74
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,240
The more I eat, the hungrier I get.

75
00:06:07,199 --> 00:06:08,000
What kind of fruit is this?

76
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:12,279
I don't know. I picked it up nearby.

77
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,600
Jumping off a building didn't kill me.

78
00:06:21,959 --> 00:06:23,040
The tiger didn't kill me.

79
00:06:24,199 --> 00:06:25,560
But now I'm getting poisoned by a chef!

80
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,199
Mr. Fang!

81
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,160
My stomach hurts!

82
00:06:30,959 --> 00:06:32,800
Help!

83
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,560
Why yell? There's no one around here.

84
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,800
How could anyone possibly save us?

85
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:38,079
We still have to yell!

86
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:41,079
We're going to die out here!

87
00:06:41,079 --> 00:06:42,199
Fang Haowen!

88
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,160
My stomach hurts!

89
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:45,839
Fang Haowen!

90
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,600
Is anyone there?

91
00:06:49,319 --> 00:06:50,079
Haozi!

92
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,199
Haozi!

93
00:07:04,959 --> 00:07:05,680
Why are you here?

94
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,720
I saw the news about you online.

95
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,839
I was terrified something happened to you.

96
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:11,040
Bought a ticket yesterday and flew over.

97
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,480
I've been looking for you day and night.

98
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,920
I finally found you.

99
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,600
When we parted ways last time, I thought

100
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:17,920
I'd never see you again in this lifetime.

101
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,240
It hurts!

102
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,439
Son.

103
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:41,920
What's wrong?

104
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,600
Mom.

105
00:07:54,319 --> 00:07:56,560
Mom.

106
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,360
Mom!

107
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:05,639
Yue'er, let me tell you...

108
00:08:05,639 --> 00:08:06,439
I was tricked.

109
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,560
Tricked how?

110
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:09,120
She per...

111
00:08:11,399 --> 00:08:12,519
She personally told me.

112
00:08:12,519 --> 00:08:13,040
She said,

113
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,519
she said she appreciated my talent,

114
00:08:16,399 --> 00:08:17,560
then turned around and sold me out.

115
00:08:18,199 --> 00:08:19,279
After everything I've been through,

116
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:20,560
I feel so wronged.

117
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,279
No one can understand me.

118
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:28,680
Haozi, from today on,

119
00:08:29,639 --> 00:08:31,040
I'll always be by your side.

120
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:35,480
No matter what

121
00:08:36,159 --> 00:08:38,120
hardships you face in life,

122
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:40,639
or any pain,

123
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,200
I'll be with you.

124
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:46,200
You'll be with me?

125
00:08:48,399 --> 00:08:49,399
What about your husband?

126
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,200
We broke up.

127
00:08:57,679 --> 00:08:58,399
Broke up?

128
00:09:00,759 --> 00:09:02,200
Then what about the baby you're carrying?

129
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,159
Actually, I've always wanted to tell you.

130
00:09:07,039 --> 00:09:08,639
This baby is...

131
00:09:10,279 --> 00:09:11,000
Is...

132
00:09:11,519 --> 00:09:12,279
Is...

133
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:13,879
Is...

134
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,679
Catch me! Catch me and I'll tell you!

135
00:09:24,279 --> 00:09:28,399
Come catch me! Come catch me!

136
00:09:30,039 --> 00:09:30,639
Haozi.

137
00:09:31,679 --> 00:09:33,440
Come catch me!

138
00:09:35,159 --> 00:09:35,519
Where did you go?

139
00:09:35,519 --> 00:09:36,440
Come catch me!

140
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,000
Come on! Catch me!

141
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:40,679
Come on!

142
00:09:43,519 --> 00:09:44,240
Mom.

143
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,440
I think I messed up.

144
00:09:47,919 --> 00:09:51,039
I fed Mr. Fang a poisonous fruit.

145
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,360
He... Look.

146
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:00,759
He looks like he's dying.

147
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:03,759
Silly kid, it's fine.

148
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,639
Look, isn't Mr. Fang alive and kicking?

149
00:10:13,519 --> 00:10:14,159
Yue'er,

150
00:10:15,799 --> 00:10:17,159
the baby you're carrying is...

151
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,279
Is...

152
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:21,519
Is really...

153
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:23,639
Is really...

154
00:10:23,639 --> 00:10:24,279
Is really...

155
00:10:35,559 --> 00:10:38,000
Looks like Mr. Fang is starving.

156
00:10:43,639 --> 00:10:44,279
Yue'er.

157
00:10:44,879 --> 00:10:46,039
His lips are a bit chapped.

158
00:10:46,759 --> 00:10:47,799
They scratched me till I bled.

159
00:10:55,759 --> 00:10:56,519
Yue'er, you go first.

160
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:58,120
I...

161
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:58,759
Go!

162
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:02,559
Come at me if you have the guts.

163
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,840
Let my wife and unborn child go.

164
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,000
Come on!

165
00:11:08,799 --> 00:11:11,080
Scared? Let's go one-on-one!

166
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,840
You ate my wife and child!

167
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,000
I'm taking you down!

168
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:34,919
Go for my throat, huh?

169
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:35,919
Go for my throat!

170
00:11:36,639 --> 00:11:38,080
I'll hit you with a body slam!

171
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,279
Bam, I'll flip you over!

172
00:11:39,279 --> 00:11:39,840
Believe me?

173
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:40,759
Are you scared?

174
00:11:40,919 --> 00:11:42,200
Spit my wife and child out!

175
00:11:42,759 --> 00:11:43,679
Spit them out!

176
00:11:47,679 --> 00:11:48,360
Freeze!

177
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,519
Evil beast, do not harm people!

178
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:12,519
Master, hurry!

179
00:12:12,519 --> 00:12:12,919
Master, hurry!

180
00:12:13,279 --> 00:12:13,919
Look.

181
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:15,559
Look.

182
00:12:20,679 --> 00:12:22,399
Patron, sorry to startle you.

183
00:12:27,919 --> 00:12:29,519
I must be dreaming. I'm... dreaming.

184
00:12:31,039 --> 00:12:31,639
You... You...

185
00:12:31,759 --> 00:12:32,039
I...

186
00:12:32,039 --> 00:12:32,200
I...

187
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,279
Where's that... where's that tiger?

188
00:12:33,279 --> 00:12:34,480
My wife and kid are still in its belly!

189
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,799
Where did that tiger go? That tiger!

190
00:12:35,799 --> 00:12:37,000
Don't panic, Patron.

191
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,480
Everything is but an illusion.

192
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:48,600
Patron, this humble monk is from
the Great Tang of the East.

193
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,519
To meet you eminent monks...

194
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,279
This...

195
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,000
What an honor!

196
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:55,399
Please rise, Patron.

197
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:56,840
I... I want to ask,

198
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,879
are you heading to the Western Heaven?

199
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:00,399
Can you take me with you?

200
00:13:00,399 --> 00:13:01,320
I can't stay here anymore.

201
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,399
I've suffered too many hardships.

202
00:13:02,399 --> 00:13:03,480
Please take me with you.

203
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:04,799
Please, Tang Monk?

204
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,240
Patron.

205
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:08,759
Life is full of hardships.

206
00:13:08,799 --> 00:13:10,000
It is a path we all must walk.

207
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:10,960
If you persevere,

208
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,840
you will eventually achieve fulfillment.

209
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:13,919
Master is right!

210
00:13:13,919 --> 00:13:16,000
I can't persevere anymore!

211
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Right now, I just want to die.

212
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:17,840
I just want to die!

213
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,159
I just want to die!

214
00:13:19,159 --> 00:13:21,639
Tang Monk, take me to the Western Heaven.

215
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,039
But, Patron,

216
00:13:24,279 --> 00:13:25,360
this humble monk's disciples

217
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,840
all have terminal illnesses.

218
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:27,600
No,

219
00:13:28,039 --> 00:13:29,279
have unique skills.

220
00:13:29,279 --> 00:13:31,960
What extraordinary abilities do you have?

221
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,840
I am but a man of letters.

222
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:37,759
Wukong, let's go.

223
00:13:37,759 --> 00:13:38,159
Let's go.

224
00:13:39,759 --> 00:13:41,840
Wait, wait, wait!

225
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,639
Okay, don't go. Don't go!

226
00:13:43,879 --> 00:13:44,960
Okay, alright, alright.

227
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,200
We're not going, not going.

228
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,799
Look, I'm just a mortal.

229
00:13:47,799 --> 00:13:48,960
But you're immortals.

230
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,279
I just have two small requests.

231
00:13:50,279 --> 00:13:51,159
Could you help me out?

232
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:52,200
Very simple. First,

233
00:13:52,679 --> 00:13:54,279
my wife and kid were eaten by a tiger.

234
00:13:54,279 --> 00:13:55,360
Could you bring my wife and kid

235
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:55,919
back for me?

236
00:13:55,919 --> 00:13:56,360
And one more thing.

237
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,600
There's a cabin on that mountain.

238
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,759
Inside is a White Bone Demon.

239
00:13:58,759 --> 00:14:00,200
Could you grab her while you're at it?

240
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:01,720
Patron,

241
00:14:02,039 --> 00:14:04,159
this humble monk cannot bring them back.

242
00:14:04,159 --> 00:14:06,840
What's done cannot be undone.

243
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,759
Aren't you Victorious Fighting Buddha
and Marshal Tianpeng?

244
00:14:10,759 --> 00:14:11,720
You can't even help with this?

245
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:13,240
We haven't got the True Scriptures yet.

246
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:14,919
Doesn't Sun Wukong know
the Seventy-Two Transformations?

247
00:14:14,919 --> 00:14:16,159
Just transform my wife and kid back.

248
00:14:16,159 --> 00:14:16,639
That should do it.

249
00:14:16,639 --> 00:14:17,279
What's wrong?

250
00:14:18,759 --> 00:14:19,480
Transform!

251
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,039
What the hell? So disgusting!

252
00:14:22,039 --> 00:14:22,600
Get lost!

253
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,279
Man, this Idiot is so demanding.

254
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,399
Who are you calling an Idiot?

255
00:14:26,399 --> 00:14:26,960
You're immortals.

256
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,720
What's wrong with helping out?

257
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,600
Why are you spouting gossip

258
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:29,320
over there?

259
00:14:29,679 --> 00:14:30,600
Don't be insolent!

260
00:14:30,799 --> 00:14:31,720
Who's being insolent?

261
00:14:32,279 --> 00:14:33,840
How dare you speak so arrogantly!

262
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,080
I did. Gonna hit me?

263
00:14:35,399 --> 00:14:37,559
You Scoundrel! Take a blow from my cudgel!

264
00:14:37,559 --> 00:14:38,440
Stop bragging!

265
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,200
Bring it on, Stable Boy!

266
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,120
Hit me right here! Come on!

267
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,759
Hit me here if you have guts! So annoying!

268
00:14:41,759 --> 00:14:42,840
Who do you think you are? Fight me!

269
00:14:42,879 --> 00:14:43,759
I dare you to touch me!

270
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,279
Senior Brother, don't hit! Don't touch me!

271
00:14:45,279 --> 00:14:46,360
Let's talk this out!

272
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,039
Senior Brother!

273
00:14:47,039 --> 00:14:48,039
Second Senior Brother is right.

274
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,679
Wukong, don't be impulsive.

275
00:14:49,679 --> 00:14:51,679
Nothing a vegetarian meal can't solve.

276
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:52,960
He is a mortal.

277
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,120
He can't understand your struggles.

278
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:54,639
Right!

279
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,440
I'm a mortal.

280
00:14:55,559 --> 00:14:56,519
You immortals, give me a hand.

281
00:14:56,519 --> 00:14:57,200
So what if I'm a mortal?

282
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:57,759
So what if you're immortals?

283
00:14:57,879 --> 00:14:58,879
So what if you're immortals?

284
00:14:58,879 --> 00:14:59,559
Especially you!

285
00:14:59,559 --> 00:15:01,000
A lustful, greedy, backstabbing pig!

286
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
And a hot-tempered monkey!

287
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:02,440
So annoying!

288
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,559
Stop acting like a Phony!

289
00:15:03,559 --> 00:15:04,320
Who are you lecturing here?

290
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,759
Who are you putting on an act for?

291
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,799
Where do you get the nerve to act with me?

292
00:15:07,799 --> 00:15:08,919
Freeze!

293
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:10,519
Beat him up!

294
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:18,519
Wujing, you hit a bit too hard just now.

295
00:15:18,919 --> 00:15:20,679
Watching it made my heart skipped a beat.

296
00:15:21,039 --> 00:15:22,080
He doesn't value me at all.

297
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,240
When he insulted my senior brothers,

298
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,480
he didn't bring me up at all!

299
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,039
It doesn't matter if he brings you up.

300
00:15:26,159 --> 00:15:27,559
Just remember to bring the luggage.

301
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,440
That monkey beat me up.

302
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:36,120
The pig beat me up.

303
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,360
Sha Monk beat me up too.

304
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:41,720
Are we done here?

305
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:45,759
Hello.

306
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,039
Please, calm down.

307
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:52,919
Do not let a moment's humiliation
disturb your mind.

308
00:15:55,759 --> 00:15:58,519
I am Confucius, Kong Zhongni.

309
00:15:58,759 --> 00:16:00,240
Kong Zhongni?

310
00:16:00,759 --> 00:16:01,720
Why are you pretending to be Confucius?

311
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:05,360
I am Zhuangzi.

312
00:16:05,759 --> 00:16:06,399
Zhuangzi?

313
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,799
Why don't you claim to be Sun Tzu?

314
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:12,000
I am Sun Tzu.

315
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,559
Then are we missing Laozi?

316
00:16:14,919 --> 00:16:16,799
I am Laozi.

317
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,080
You really cleared my meridians.

318
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,000
No, what are you doing?

319
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,080
Do I even know you?

320
00:16:20,759 --> 00:16:21,759
Dazzling white.

321
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:23,240
You're a white... white-bearded old man.

322
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,679
You're dazzling white, you really are...

323
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,279
A gentleman remains steadfast in adversity.

324
00:16:27,559 --> 00:16:29,159
A petty person becomes reckless in poverty.

325
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,320
The humiliation of cyberbullying,

326
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:31,320
The pain of heartbreak,

327
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,919
Are all earthly illusions.

328
00:16:32,919 --> 00:16:34,440
You must govern by non-action.

329
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:36,600
Heartbreak is like facing an enemy.

330
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,600
Treat it like commanding an army.

331
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,879
It's an opportunity to temper your mind.

332
00:16:39,879 --> 00:16:40,840
Follow the course of nature,

333
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:41,440
Avoid the enemy's edge,

334
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,679
And do not cling to pain.

335
00:16:42,679 --> 00:16:43,840
Engage actively with the world.

336
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:44,919
Roam freely in the world,
and gather your strength.

337
00:16:44,919 --> 00:16:45,600
By not contending, one is beyond contention.

338
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,080
You must...

339
00:16:51,879 --> 00:16:52,759
Oh my God!

340
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:53,840
Don't give me that!

341
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:55,000
Stop pretending to be...

342
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,879
Confucius, Laozi, Zhuangzi, and Sun Tzu!

343
00:16:57,159 --> 00:16:58,320
What's this got to do with you, Sadako?

344
00:16:58,519 --> 00:16:59,200
Go back!

345
00:16:59,639 --> 00:17:00,639
Scram, scram, scram!

346
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,160
Bie Fan

347
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:21,559
Bie Fan

348
00:17:22,839 --> 00:17:23,559
Bie Fan

349
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,079
Did you run into the tiger too?

350
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,319
No.

351
00:17:51,559 --> 00:17:53,039
Do you like the starry sky too?

352
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,240
I'm Fang Haowen.

353
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,279
A man of letters.

354
00:17:58,559 --> 00:17:59,759
We're fellow artists.

355
00:18:01,319 --> 00:18:02,200
I'm Vincent van Gogh.

356
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:03,519
Who?

357
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:04,079
Vincent van Gogh.

358
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:05,640
Vin... Vin...

359
00:18:06,799 --> 00:18:07,519
Vincent van Gogh.

360
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,680
You're Vincent van Gogh?

361
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:15,160
Oh my God! I get to meet Vincent van Gogh!

362
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,880
And it seems I can... can understand you.

363
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:30,920
Your ear.

364
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,000
Where's my ear?

365
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,519
A tiger took it.

366
00:18:34,039 --> 00:18:34,880
What about your ear?

367
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:37,480
I cut it off for the woman I love.

368
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:39,119
She must've been very touched.

369
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:39,799
No.

370
00:18:39,799 --> 00:18:40,839
She told me to get lost.

371
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:43,680
W-why did you give her your ear?

372
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,799
I wanted her to hear my heart.

373
00:18:45,799 --> 00:18:47,599
Then she should've given you hers.

374
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:50,839
I didn't think of that.

375
00:18:52,359 --> 00:18:53,119
You know me?

376
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,119
I do. But not just me.

377
00:18:55,119 --> 00:18:56,279
It's not just me who knows you.

378
00:18:56,599 --> 00:18:58,000
The whole world knows you.

379
00:18:58,119 --> 00:18:59,079
They love you.

380
00:18:59,519 --> 00:19:01,279
They're all crazy about you.

381
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:03,400
But when I was alive...

382
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,559
Why didn't anyone love me?

383
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:05,680
What do they love about me?

384
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,119
They love your paintings.

385
00:19:09,559 --> 00:19:10,599
Do you remember painting one...

386
00:19:10,599 --> 00:19:11,839
called Sunflowers?

387
00:19:12,839 --> 00:19:14,039
It sold for 100 million last year.

388
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,079
US dollars.

389
00:19:19,359 --> 00:19:22,119
That could buy a lot of leather shoes.

390
00:19:34,279 --> 00:19:35,319
Before, my paintings

391
00:19:35,319 --> 00:19:37,039
couldn't even buy a bag of potatoes.

392
00:19:42,759 --> 00:19:45,519
They took my *The Potato Eaters*

393
00:19:45,759 --> 00:19:46,799
and hung it in the bathroom.

394
00:19:50,799 --> 00:19:52,079
At least they still bought your paintings.

395
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:59,519
I sold one painting for 400 francs.

396
00:19:59,519 --> 00:20:00,279
Do you know why?

397
00:20:02,119 --> 00:20:02,799
Why?

398
00:20:03,519 --> 00:20:04,920
Because the buyer was drunk.

399
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:10,839
They have drunkards abroad too?

400
00:20:11,039 --> 00:20:12,200
Quite a few drunkards, actually.

401
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:17,480
He must've made a fortune by now.

402
00:20:22,039 --> 00:20:22,799
Let me ask you something.

403
00:20:22,799 --> 00:20:23,400
Since

404
00:20:24,599 --> 00:20:26,000
your paintings couldn't buy potatoes,

405
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:29,039
why did you keep painting?

406
00:20:29,559 --> 00:20:31,319
Because these colors screamed in my veins.

407
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,640
If I didn't paint them,

408
00:20:32,759 --> 00:20:33,559
they'd split my bones

409
00:20:33,559 --> 00:20:34,519
and burst through my skin.

410
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:38,480
What about you?

411
00:20:38,599 --> 00:20:39,480
Why do you write books?

412
00:20:41,119 --> 00:20:43,160
Can your books buy you potatoes?

413
00:21:02,319 --> 00:21:03,720
The moon is a triangle.

414
00:21:05,279 --> 00:21:06,319
You found me.

415
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:08,720
Who are you?

416
00:21:10,319 --> 00:21:11,559
Tencent Video.

417
00:21:12,519 --> 00:21:13,799
Why are you airing this show?

418
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,799
Because we want to bring the audience joy.

419
00:21:16,559 --> 00:21:17,160
Can you?

420
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,400
We can. Look at the danmaku.

421
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:19,640
Dan-what?

422
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:20,839
Danmaku.

423
00:21:36,839 --> 00:21:37,680
Thank you.

424
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:39,119
It's been over 130 years.

425
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:41,039
You're the only one who'll listen to me.

426
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,480
This gift is for you.

427
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:46,039
This...

428
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,680
You're not giving me a painting?

429
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:09,920
The truth is, I don't have much

430
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:11,079
to give you.

431
00:22:11,839 --> 00:22:12,920
Then give me a poem.

432
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:17,759
You got it.

433
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:29,160
Some write poetry with passion,

434
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:31,759
stopping purely at the level of feeling.

435
00:22:33,079 --> 00:22:35,440
Yet it makes water drops surge

436
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:38,920
and flames burn fiercely.

437
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:39,920
Some

438
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:42,200
write poetry with talent.

439
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:43,680
Before they even try,

440
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:46,160
their words are already lofty,

441
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:49,200
stunningly arrogant.

442
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:50,720
Some

443
00:22:51,599 --> 00:22:53,160
write poetry with their brains,

444
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:55,160
shrewdly manipulating words.

445
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,880
Every sentence is twisted into poetry

446
00:22:58,319 --> 00:22:59,920
before it's allowed on stage.

447
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:01,160
Some

448
00:23:02,599 --> 00:23:03,920
write poetry with their hearts.

449
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:07,119
Unbearable joy and pain

450
00:23:07,359 --> 00:23:08,559
are, in the process,

451
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,240
completely dissolved.

452
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,319
No matter how fierce the impulse,

453
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,440
it ultimately returns to calm.

454
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,839
Some, since they began writing poetry,

455
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:21,759
grow thinner day by day.

456
00:23:22,599 --> 00:23:23,680
Every single word

457
00:23:24,519 --> 00:23:27,640
is mass torn from their bodies.

458
00:23:28,079 --> 00:23:29,759
People like this write poetry

459
00:23:31,759 --> 00:23:32,880
with their lives.

460
00:25:33,559 --> 00:25:34,839
Oh no, I'm out of tune.

461
00:25:35,039 --> 00:25:36,920
I can't hear you! I can't hear you!
I can't hear you!

462
00:25:52,599 --> 00:25:53,720
Mom.

463
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:56,119
You're drooling.

464
00:25:56,720 --> 00:25:58,359
Why is there so much?

465
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:16,960
You can't see me. Can't... can't see me.

466
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:22,319
You can't see me.

467
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:35,400
M- Mr. Fang.

468
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:36,000
Yeah.

469
00:26:39,119 --> 00:26:39,759
Run!

470
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:43,079
Hurry up!

471
00:26:43,079 --> 00:26:43,720
Calm down!

472
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:26,400
Mr. Fang, is that long thing a bug?

473
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:28,920
What bug? It's poop.

474
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:30,880
Did you poop that?

475
00:27:30,960 --> 00:27:31,880
What would I even poop out?

476
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:32,519
Have I even eaten anything?

477
00:27:32,519 --> 00:27:33,720
To be able to poop that much?

478
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:36,000
That's not my poop!
